14
00:00:48.799 --> 00:00:54.799
So we're going to transform what used to be our crew into an entire CrewAI flow now.

15
00:00:54.799 --> 00:00:57.279
And just to remember where we left off,

16
00:00:57.279 --> 00:01:02.880
we end up with our research crew being a hybrid approach where you had a research planner

17
00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:07.360
that would do an entire hypothesis on how he would break up our questions

18
00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:09.120
and what are the things that we should research.

19
00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:11.839
That would trigger two different tasks.

20
00:01:11.839 --> 00:01:16.720
One to research a main topic, another one to research a secondary topic,

21
00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:20.239
but only one agent would be doing those same tasks.

22
00:01:20.239 --> 00:01:24.239
And then that would go into fact checking where the same thing would happen.

23
00:01:24.239 --> 00:01:28.080
One agent would be doing the two fact checking as well for us.

24
00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:31.760
And then from that point, everything would collapse back

25
00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:35.839
into writing a final report with our final report agent.

26
00:01:35.839 --> 00:01:39.279
So this is where we left when we last talked about this.

27
00:01:39.279 --> 00:01:43.199
And we're using the guardrails, the custom tools and the memories,

28
00:01:43.199 --> 00:01:45.519
everything that we have learned into this.

29
00:01:45.519 --> 00:01:49.919
But now we're taking it to the next level by using Crew AI Flows.

30
00:01:50.639 --> 00:01:53.839
So the idea of our crew, it still exists in there.

31
00:01:53.839 --> 00:01:56.559
And that still runs the same way that it used to.

32
00:01:56.559 --> 00:01:59.760
We're not changing anything about it up to this point.

33
00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:03.199
But we are changing the way that we get to that process.

34
00:02:03.199 --> 00:02:06.239
So now the user will be able to start the conversation

35
00:02:06.239 --> 00:02:09.520
being vocal about what it wants to learn about.

36
00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:11.199
And this can be literally anything.

37
00:02:11.199 --> 00:02:15.279
The user can just say hello, or it can say anything else.

38
00:02:15.279 --> 00:02:19.360
Maybe he wants to learn about the origin of the universe or whatever it might be.

39
00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:23.679
And from this point on, we're going to do one single ad hoc LLM call.

40
00:02:23.679 --> 00:02:28.080
That we try to make a decision whether we need to trigger a research or not.

41
00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:30.559
And if we don't need to trigger a research,

42
00:02:30.559 --> 00:02:34.720
we're just going to generate an answer to the LLM and return that answer right away.

43
00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:41.279
Now, if we do want to do the research that will execute and trigger our entire crew,

44
00:02:41.279 --> 00:02:46.559
that will then ask for clarifying questions and give a final summary

45
00:02:46.559 --> 00:02:49.360
that will return that answer back to us.

46
00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:53.360
So you can see how this now is a little more complex.

47
00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:59.039
But also allow us to have way more control over what is happening and when it's happening.

48
00:02:59.039 --> 00:03:03.679
And what I'm very excited about this is that this is extremely easy to build.

49
00:03:03.679 --> 00:03:06.720
Because flows is just a very thin layer.

50
00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:09.600
It just gives you the bare minimum to make sure that you get

51
00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:12.160
everything that you need to build these automations

52
00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:15.919
by using a series of decorators that make your life super easy.

53
00:03:15.919 --> 00:03:19.839
So I'm very excited to get our hands dirty and see what that looks like.

54
00:03:19.839 --> 00:03:21.520
So let's jump into that right away.

55
00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:26.800
The first thing that I want to call out here is that for you to create initial flow,

