00:03:32.559 --> 00:03:38.479
all you got to do is using the CrewAI CLI and type crewai create flow.

59
00:03:38.479 --> 00:03:40.240
And you can give your flow a name.

60
00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:44.160
So in this case, I would do just a task flow here to showcase.

61
00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:50.320
Once that you create this, it will create the entire scaffold and folder structure for you,

62
00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:52.399
setting up everything that you need.

63
00:03:52.399 --> 00:03:55.759
And if you go into that folder, as we can do right now,

64
00:03:55.759 --> 00:03:57.440
you can actually see what that looks like.

65
00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:02.960
So it will have not only a regular pyproject and readme file and .env,

66
00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:06.479
but we'll have an src and a test folder.

67
00:04:06.479 --> 00:04:11.039
And if you go into that SRC folder, you're going to find our flow.

68
00:04:11.039 --> 00:04:16.160
In that flow, you're going to have a main.py file that holds the code for your flow.

